WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.501 line:0%
- The president has been in
office barely three weeks.

00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:04.370 line:0%
Why can't you guys in
the media and Hollywood

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:06.572 line:7%
give him some slack?

00:00:06.673 --> 00:00:08.574 line:0%
BILL MAHER: Because of
what he's done and said.

00:00:08.674 --> 00:00:09.408 line:7%
[interposing voices]

00:00:09.508 --> 00:00:10.577 line:7%
- [inaudible] only three weeks.

00:00:10.677 --> 00:00:11.377 line:7%
BILL MAHER: Three weeks?

00:00:11.477 --> 00:00:12.312 line:7%
- Give him a break.

00:00:12.412 --> 00:00:13.212 line:7%
Can't you give him a break?

00:00:13.312 --> 00:00:14.681 line:7%
BILL MAHER: Give him a break?

00:00:14.781 --> 00:00:15.481 line:7%
Do you read the news?

00:00:15.581 --> 00:00:16.482 line:7%
Do you--

00:00:16.582 --> 00:00:17.817 line:0%
- --which is the
toughest job on earth?

00:00:17.917 --> 00:00:19.085 line:0%
BILL MAHER: The
toughest job on earth

00:00:19.185 --> 00:00:20.687 line:7%
has never been done like this.

00:00:20.787 --> 00:00:22.855 line:0%
First of all, this is beyond
the realm of politics.

00:00:22.955 --> 00:00:24.323 line:0%
If you're just talking
about politics--

00:00:24.423 --> 00:00:26.593 line:0%
OK, let's pretend that
it's just politics.

00:00:26.693 --> 00:00:30.329 line:0%
I would have big problems
there, because it's a giant con,

00:00:30.429 --> 00:00:31.230 line:7%
what he's done.

00:00:31.330 --> 00:00:32.798 line:7%
He ran for the little man.

00:00:32.898 --> 00:00:33.699 line:7%
And then what does he do?

00:00:33.799 --> 00:00:34.900 line:7%
He gets into office.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:38.037 line:0%
The coal companies can
dump sludge in the river,

00:00:38.137 --> 00:00:41.974 line:0%
because you know, that's what
the little man is aching for.

00:00:42.074 --> 00:00:44.977 line:0%
Undoing Dodd-Frank, because
so many of the town halls

00:00:45.077 --> 00:00:47.379 line:0%
in Appalachia, people were
standing up and saying,

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:51.517 line:0%
Mr. Trump, please get
rid of the Volcker Rule.

00:00:51.617 --> 00:00:54.420 line:0%
Because if I can't make certain
speculative investments,

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:56.555 line:7%
it's killing us here.

00:00:56.655 --> 00:00:58.190 line:0%
So that's just the
political part.

00:00:58.291 --> 00:01:00.460 line:0%
We could have a normal
conversation about that.

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:02.828 line:0%
But this presidency is not
about the political part,

00:01:02.928 --> 00:01:04.264 line:7%
even three weeks in.

00:01:04.364 --> 00:01:05.798 line:7%
It's beyond politics.

00:01:05.898 --> 00:01:07.166 line:7%
It's about sanity.

00:01:07.266 --> 00:01:11.437 line:0%
It's about somebody who makes
stuff up, who doesn't read.

00:01:11.537 --> 00:01:14.007 line:0%
His information is
either anecdotal

00:01:14.107 --> 00:01:16.142 line:7%
or pulled right out of his--

00:01:16.242 --> 00:01:17.877 line:7%
what word, Reverend, should I--

00:01:17.977 --> 00:01:18.678 line:7%
his behind.

00:01:21.981 --> 00:01:24.083 line:0%
Of course, we're worried
when the president

00:01:24.183 --> 00:01:26.552 line:0%
sees multitudes
that don't exist,

00:01:26.652 --> 00:01:30.155 line:7%
as in the illegal voting--

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:31.324 line:7%
3 million.

00:01:31.424 --> 00:01:32.957 line:7%
That should bother you.

